# Copied into the plan repo as `.gitignore` before any file with content in it
# exists. Every line carries its reason, because a rule nobody can justify is a
# rule somebody deletes six commits later.

# The seed. One person's own words about who they want, including whatever they
# wrote before they thought about it being read. Attached to a real name it is
# permanent and public. The decode cites it by line number and never quotes it.
seed.md

# The likeness files. These name other people — friends, family, exes — who did
# not agree to be in a document. The exposure here is theirs, not yours.
likeness-*.md

# The interview answers: place, timetable, free evenings, dealbreakers. A map of
# where one person is on a Wednesday.
interview.md

# The ledger. Dates and rooms is a movement history.
log.tsv

# The calendar. The same movement history, in a format other software reads.
*.ics

# Outbound drafts. Half-written mail about a real person is worse than sent mail
# about one.
outreach/

# Photographs and their metadata. Raw camera files carry the GPS of wherever
# they were taken, including home. Run strip_exif.py before any of these leave.
photos/
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.heic

# Scratch.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
